e of orphan</em> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 5:28\" href=\"/Jeremiah.5.28\">Je 5:28</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">ד׳ דין עני ואביון</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 22:16\" href=\"/Jeremiah.22.16\">Je 22:16</a>; also acc. cogn. om., <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 31:9\" href=\"/Proverbs.31.9\">Pr 31:9</a>."}], "num": "a."}, {"senses": [{"definition": "of God, <span dir=\"rtl\">דָּנַנִּי אֱלֹהִים</span> <em>God has pled my cause</em> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 30:6\" href=\"/Genesis.30.6\">Gn 30:6</a> (E)."}], "num": "b."}], "num": "2."}, {"senses": [{"definition": "<em>execute judgment, vindicate</em>, in battle against enemies, <span dir=\"rtl\">דָּן יָדִין עַמּוֹ</span> <em>Dan will judge</em> (vindicate as a warrior) <em>his people</em> (v. Di) <a data-ref=\"Genesis 49:16\" href=\"/Genesis.49.16\">Gn 49:16</a> (poet.); the Messianic king <span dir=\"rtl\">בגוים</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 110:6\" href=\"/Psalms.110.6\">ψ 110:6</a>; God, <span dir=\"rtl\">בִּגְבוּרָֽתְךָ תְדִינֵנִי</span> <em>in thy might judge me</em> (vindicate me) <a data-ref=\"Psalms 54:3\" href=\"/Psalms.54.3\">ψ 54:3</a>."}], "num": "3."}, {"senses": [{"definition": "<em>execute judgment, requite</em>, of man, <span dir=\"rtl\">דִּינוּ לַבֹּקֶר מִשְׁפָּט</span> <em>execute judgment every morning</em> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 21:12\" href=\"/Jeremiah.21.12\">Je 21:12</a>; of God, upon Egypt <a data-ref=\"Genesis 15:14\" href=\"/Genesis.15.14\">Gn 15:14</a> (E); <span dir=\"rtl\">עמים</span> by means of powers of nature <a data-ref=\"Job 36:31\" href=\"/Job.36.31\">Jb 36:31</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אפסי ארץ</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 2:10\" href=\"/I_Samuel.2.10\">1 S 2:10</a> (poet.)"}], "num": "4."}, {"senses": [{"definition": "<em>govern</em>, <span dir=\"rtl\">אַתָּה תָּדִין אֶת־בֵּיתִי</span> <em>thou shalt govern my house</em> <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 3:7\" href=\"/Zechariah.3.7\">Zc 3:7</a>."}], "num": "5."}, {"senses": [{"definition": "<span dir=\"rtl\">לֹא־יוּכַל לָדִין עִם</span> <em>he cannot contend with</em> one mightier than he <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 6:10\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.6.10\">Ec 6:10</a>."}], "num": "6."}], "form": "Qal"}, {"senses": [{"definition": "<em>Pt.</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">וַיְהִי כָל־הָעָם נָדוֹן בְּכָל־שִׁבְטֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל</span> <em>and all the people were at strife througout all the tribes of Israel</em> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 19:10\" href=\"/II_Samuel.19.10\">2 S 19:10</a> (reciprocal, cf. Dr.)"}], "form": "Niph."}, {"definition": "—<span dir=\"rtl\">לֹא־יָדוֹן רוּחִי בָֽאָדָם לְעֹלָם</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 6:3\" href=\"/Genesis.6.3\">Gn 6:3</a> cp. perhaps <span dir=\"rtl\">دان</span> <em>continue, do</em> something <em>continually</em>, in mod. Egyptian Arabic (So<sup>SK lxvii (1894), 211 f.</sup>).is difficult. (1) 𝔊 𝔙 𝔖 Onk read <span dir=\"rtl\">ידור</span> or (Kue) <span dir=\"rtl\">ילון</span> <em>abide in, dwell,—My spirit will not abide in man for ever;</em> this best suits the context, but <span dir=\"rtl\">ידור</span>, as Aramaism, is dub. (2) Kn De Schr RVm render <em>rule in</em>, supported by <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 3:7\" href=\"/Zechariah.3.7\">Zc 3:7</a> only. (3) Thes Ew Di render <em>be humbled in</em>, sustained by Arabic, not Heb., usage. (4) <em>strive with</em> of AV RV (cf. <strong>6</strong> supr.) is not justified. <span dir=\"rtl\">יָדוֹן</span>", "note": true}]}, "rid": "BDB02120", "strong_numbers": ["1777", "1778", "1779", "1780"], "next_hw": "דִּין²", "prev_hw": "דִּימוֹנָה", "all_cited": true, "root": true, "quotes": [], "GK": ["1878", "1906", "1907"], "TWOT": ["2674", "426", "426a"], "parent_lexicon_details": {"name": "BDB Dictionary", "language": "heb.biblical", "to_language": "eng", "text_categories": [], "source": "BDB Dictionary", "attribution": "F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs", "index_title": "BDB", "version_title": "A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906", "version_lang": "en", "should_autocomplete"