:25\" href=\"/Numbers.10.25\">10:25</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 26:42\" href=\"/Numbers.26.42\">26:42</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 34:22\" href=\"/Numbers.34.22\">34:22</a> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 19:40\" href=\"/Joshua.19.40\">Jos 19:40</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 19:47\" href=\"/Joshua.19.47\">47</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 19:48\" href=\"/Joshua.19.48\">48</a> (all P) <a data-ref=\"Judges 1:34\" href=\"/Judges.1.34\">Ju 1:34</a> <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:2\" href=\"/Judges.18.2\">18:2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:16\" href=\"/Judges.18.16\">16</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:22\" href=\"/Judges.18.22\">22</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:23\" href=\"/Judges.18.23\">23</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:25\" href=\"/Judges.18.25\">25</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:26\" href=\"/Judges.18.26\">26</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:30\" href=\"/Judges.18.30\">30</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מַחֲנֵה דָן</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 2:25\" href=\"/Numbers.2.25\">Nu 2:25</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 2:31\" href=\"/Numbers.2.31\">31</a> (P)—on <a data-ref=\"Judges 13:25\" href=\"/Judges.13.25\">Ju 13:25</a>; <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:12\" href=\"/Judges.18.12\">18:12</a> v. <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, מַחֲנֶה²\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_מַחֲנֶה²\">מַחֲנֶה</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מִשְׁפְּחֹת דָּן</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 26:42\" href=\"/Numbers.26.42\">Nu 26:42</a> (P); <span dir=\"rtl\">דָּן</span> alone in poetry <a data-ref=\"Genesis 49:16\" href=\"/Genesis.49.16\">Gn 49:16</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 49:17\" href=\"/Genesis.49.17\">17</a> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 33:22\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.33.22\">Dt 33:22</a><sup>(×2)</sup> <a data-ref=\"Judges 5:17\" href=\"/Judges.5.17\">Ju 5:17</a>, elsewhere <a data-ref=\"Numbers 1:12\" href=\"/Numbers.1.12\">Nu 1:12</a> (P) <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 27:13\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.27.13\">Dt 27:13</a> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 27:22\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.27.22\">1 Ch 27:22</a> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 2:13\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.2.13\">2 Ch 2:13</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 48:1\" href=\"/Ezekiel.48.1\">Ez 48:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 48:2\" href=\"/Ezekiel.48.2\">2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 48:32\" href=\"/Ezekiel.48.32\">32</a>."}], "num": "2."}, {"senses": [{"definition": "a city on northern frontier of Israel at one of the sources of the Jordan, originally <span dir=\"rtl\">לַיִשׁ</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:29\" href=\"/Judges.18.29\">Ju 18:29</a> (cf. v <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:7\" href=\"/Judges.18.7\">7</a>); = <span dir=\"rtl\">לָשֶׁם</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 19:47\" href=\"/Joshua.19.47\">Jos 19:47</a>; captured by a colony of Danites; named Dan, and made a sacred place with rites of worship that lasted until the exile (<a data-ref=\"Judges 18:30\" href=\"/Judges.18.30\">Ju 18:30</a>); =<em>Tell el Kâdî</em>, Rob<sup>BR iii. 351, 358</sup> Bd<sup>Pal 265</sup>. This place is frequently referred to: <a data-ref=\"Genesis 14:14\" href=\"/Genesis.14.14\">Gn 14:14</a> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 34:1\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.34.1\">Dt 34:1</a> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 12:29\" href=\"/I_Kings.12.29\">1 K 12:29</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 12:30\" href=\"/I_Kings.12.30\">30</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 15:20\" href=\"/I_Kings.15.20\">15:20</a> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 10:29\" href=\"/II_Kings.10.29\">2 K 10:29</a> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 16:4\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.16.4\">2 Ch 16:4</a> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 4:15\" href=\"/Jeremiah.4.15\">Je 4:15</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 8:16\" href=\"/Jeremiah.8.16\">8:16</a> <a data-ref=\"Amos 8:14\" href=\"/Amos.8.14\">Am 8:14</a>: read also <span dir=\"rtl\">וּבְדָן</span> for <span dir=\"rtl\">וְכֵן</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 20:18\" href=\"/II_Samuel.20.18\">2 S 20:18</a> 𝔊 Ew We cf. Dr; and v. the phrase <span dir=\"rtl\">מִדָּן וְעַד־בְּאֵר שֶׁבַע</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 20:1\" href=\"/Judges.20.1\">Ju 20:1</a> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 3:20\" href=\"/I_Samuel.3.20\">1 S 3:20</a> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 3:10\" href=\"/II_Samuel.3.10\">2 S 3:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 17:11\" href=\"/II_Samuel.17.11\">17:11</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 24:2\" href=\"/II_Samuel.24.2\">24:2</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 24:15\" href=\"/II_Samuel.24.15\">15</a> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 5:5\" href=\"/I_Kings.5.5\">1 K 5:5</a>; given by Chr <span dir=\"rtl\">מִבְּאֵר שֶׁכַע וְעַד־דָּן</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 21:2\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.21.2\">1 Ch 21:2</a> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 30:5\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.30.5\">2 Ch 30:5</a>. (<a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:19\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.19\">Ez 27:19</a> v. <span dir=\"rtl\">ודן</span>.)"}], "num": "3."}, {"definition": "—<span dir=\"rtl\">דָּ֫נָה יַעַן</span> or <span dir=\"rtl\">דַּנָֿה</span> (Bear) <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 24:6\" href=\"/II_Samuel.24.6\">2 S 24:6</a>. No such place known; text usually regarded as corrupt,and, 𝔊 being uncertain, variously changed: (1) <span dir=\"rtl\">דָּ֫נָה יַעַר</span> <em>to Dan in the wood</em>, Thes after 𝔙 <em>silvestria</em>. (2) <span dir=\"rtl\">(וַיָּסֹבּוּ) דָּ֫נָה וְעִיּוֹן</span> <em>to Dan and Ijon</em> Klo (cf. <a data-ref=\"I Kings 15:20\" href=\"/I_Kings.15.20\">1 K 15:20</a>). (3) <span dir=\"rtl\">(סָֽבֲבוּ) דָּן וּמִדָּן</span> We Dr cf. 𝔊.", "note": true}]}, "rid": "BDB02123", "strong_numbers": ["1835"], "next_hw": "דָּנִי", "prev_hw": "דִּינָה", "all_cited": true, "quotes": [], "GK": ["1968", "1969"], "TWOT": [], "parent_lexicon_details": {"name": "BDB Dictionary", "language": "heb.biblical", "to_language": "eng", "text_categories": [], "source": "BDB Dictionary", "attribution": "F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs", "index_title": "BDB", "version_title": "A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906", "version_lang": "en", "should_autocomplete": true}}, {"headword": "דָּן²", "parent_lexicon": "BDB Dictionary", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": "v. sub <a data-ref=\"BDB, דָּן\" href=\"/BDB,_דָּן\", dir=\"rtl\">דין</a>."}]}, "rid": "BD